{%- comment -%}
  sections/main-product-cowork.liquid
  Enriched PDP — Cowork enrichment layered onto standard product data.
  Ported from the standalone prototype (see enriched-pdp_2.html in the
  repo root) and built against the session brief
  (claude-code-session-brief.md).

  DATA MODEL
  ----------
  Base product fields come from the standard Liquid `product` object
  (title, vendor, images, price, variants). The single sandbox variant
  ($89, Default Title) renders as-is — frame/size selectors below are
  visible-but-static placeholder UI matching the prototype scope.

  Cowork enrichment lives in the `cowork` metafield namespace:
    cowork.summary  — single_line_text_field — plain string
    cowork.subject  — list.single_line_text_field
    cowork.style    — list.single_line_text_field
    cowork.palette  — list.single_line_text_field
    cowork.mood     — list.single_line_text_field
    cowork.keywords — list.single_line_text_field

  The five list-type fields hold a list with a single pipe-delimited
  string (quirk of how the Cowork pipeline writes them). Access pattern:
    metafield.value | first | split: '|'
  Plain `metafield.value` on a list type returns the array, not the
  string — so `| first` to get the inner string, then `| split: '|'`
  to get the tokens.

  Two prototype <-> Shopify name renames worth knowing if you cross-
  reference the prototype's data object:
    prototype `subjectTags` == Shopify `cowork.keywords`
    prototype `category`    == Shopify `cowork.subject`

  Artist data is per-product and lives in the `artist` metafield
  namespace (convention for the production port — see
  PORT-TO-PRODUCTION-PDP.md):
    artist.name      — single_line_text_field — display name
    artist.bio       — multi_line_text_field  — short bio
    artist.shop_url  — url — link to artist's storefront/profile
    artist.avatar    — url — direct image URL (sandbox uses a hot-linked
                       society6.com CDN URL; production should switch
                       this to a file_reference and host the image)

  None of those metafields are populated on Cat Landscape 154 today.
  The Meet the Artist block is gated on `artist.bio` and renders
  nothing (no empty section, no placeholder) when bio is absent. The
  byline ("By <artist>") is gated on `artist.name`. This is correct,
  not a bug — see the brief, Step 2a.

  GRACEFUL DEGRADATION
  --------------------
  Every Cowork-driven block hides cleanly when its metafield is blank:
  Aesthetic chips, palette swatches, About This Piece, Meet the Artist.
  The only always-present sections are template-static (Specifications,
  Shipping & Returns) per the brief.

  CURATION
  --------
  Per Step 4 of the brief, the page renders a curated subset of tags,
  not the full ~35-tag set:
    Style    — first 3 from cowork.style
    Mood     — first 2 from cowork.mood
    Subject  — first 3 from cowork.keywords  (yes, keywords -> Subject)
    Palette  — swatches for tokens that match a known-color hex map;
               anything else (e.g. "monochrome", "warm") becomes the
               inline palette caption.
  The full strings stay in the metafields; only the curated subset
  shows on the page AND in the JSON-LD additionalProperty (consistency
  rule from the brief: schema mirrors what's visible).

  Note: the prototype's exact label set for this product happened to
  drop "illustration" from style and "playful/elegant" from mood as
  near-duplicates. Algorithmic first-N matches the prototype on
  Subject and Palette; on Style and Mood the first-N approach will
  emit slightly different labels than the prototype's hand-curated
  list. That trade-off is deliberate — algorithmic curation is
  portable across the whole catalog; hand-curating per product is
  not. Production may want a smarter "skip near-duplicate" rule;
  flag in PORT-TO-PRODUCTION-PDP.md.

  SCOPE
  -----
  - Variants visible-but-static (prototype scope, agreed).
  - Chip hrefs are placeholders. Real collection routing is a
    production-discovery question (see brief's "Known production gaps").
  - "More like this" is a stub flagged as a production gap.

  CSS class prefix `.s6cw-` is intentional (collision-free namespace)
  and must be preserved on the production port.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # ---- Cowork enrichment reads ----
  assign cw_summary    = product.metafields.cowork.summary.value
  assign style_raw     = product.metafields.cowork.style.value
  assign mood_raw      = product.metafields.cowork.mood.value
  assign keywords_raw  = product.metafields.cowork.keywords.value
  assign palette_raw   = product.metafields.cowork.palette.value

  # ---- Artist data reads ----
  assign artist_name   = product.metafields.artist.name.value
  assign artist_bio    = product.metafields.artist.bio.value
  assign artist_avatar = product.metafields.artist.avatar.value
  assign artist_url    = product.metafields.artist.shop_url.value

  # ---- Curation counts ----
  assign style_take   = 3
  assign mood_take    = 2
  assign subject_take = 3

  # ---- JSON-LD additionalProperty accumulator (string of JSON objects) ----
  assign jsonld_props = ''
-%}

<article class="s6cw-page" data-product-id="{{ product.id }}">

  <nav class="s6cw-wrap s6cw-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a>
    <span>/</span>
    {%- if product.product_type != blank -%}
      {%- assign type_handle = product.product_type | handleize -%}
      <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/{{ type_handle }}">{{ product.product_type }}</a>
      <span>/</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {{ product.title }}
  </nav>

  <main class="s6cw-wrap">
    <div class="s6cw-product">

      {%- comment -%} ===== GALLERY ===== {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="s6cw-gallery">
        <div class="s6cw-gallery-main">
          {%- if product.featured_image -%}
            <img
              id="s6cwHero"
              src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
              alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
              width="1200"
              height="1200"
              loading="eager">
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if product.images.size > 1 -%}
          <div class="s6cw-thumbs" id="s6cwThumbs">
            {%- for img in product.images limit: 6 -%}
              <img
                src="{{ img | image_url: width: 144 }}"
                data-full="{{ img | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
                alt="{{ img.alt | default: product.title | escape }} — view {{ forloop.index }}"
                width="72"
                height="72"
                class="{% if forloop.first %}is-active{% endif %}">
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ===== BUY COLUMN ===== {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="s6cw-buy">
        <h1 class="s6cw-title">{{ product.title }}</h1>

        {%- if artist_name != blank -%}
          <div class="s6cw-byline">
            By
            {%- if artist_url != blank -%}
              <a href="{{ artist_url }}">{{ artist_name }}</a>
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="s6cw-byline-name">{{ artist_name }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="s6cw-price">{{ product.price | money }}</div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Variant selectors: visible-but-static per prototype scope.
          The sandbox product carries a single Default Title variant —
          we render the prototype's frame/size chip groups as
          presentational UI only. NOT wired to real variants. If
          variants are added in admin, swap this block for a real
          variant picker (Horizon's default <variant-picker> works
          fine in a product context).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="s6cw-opt">
          <div class="s6cw-opt-label">Frame: <b>Framed Canvas</b></div>
          <div class="s6cw-chips-row">
            <button type="button" class="s6cw-pick is-active" aria-pressed="true">Framed Canvas</button>
            <button type="button" class="s6cw-pick" aria-pressed="false">No Frame</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="s6cw-opt">
          <div class="s6cw-opt-label">Size: <b>Small 8" × 10"</b></div>
          <div class="s6cw-chips-row">
            <button type="button" class="s6cw-pick is-active" aria-pressed="true">Small 8" × 10"</button>
            <button type="button" class="s6cw-pick" aria-pressed="false">Medium 16" × 20"</button>
            <button type="button" class="s6cw-pick" aria-pressed="false">Large 24" × 30"</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- form 'product', product, class: 's6cw-cart-form' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
          <button type="submit" class="s6cw-cart"{% unless product.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
            {%- if product.available -%}Add to Cart{%- else -%}Sold Out{%- endif -%}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}

        <div class="s6cw-reassure">
          <span>Made to order — typically ships in 3–4 business days.</span>
          <span>Easy 30-day returns.</span>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} ===== ENRICHMENT 1: AESTHETIC ===== {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture aesthetic_inner -%}

          {%- comment -%} ---- STYLE ---- {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if style_raw != blank -%}
            {%- assign style_tokens = style_raw | first | split: '|' -%}
            {%- assign style_count = 0 -%}
            {%- capture style_chips -%}
              {%- for tok in style_tokens -%}
                {%- if style_count >= style_take -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign trimmed = tok | strip -%}
                {%- if trimmed == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- capture label -%}{%- render 's6cw-titlecase', token: trimmed -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- assign label = label | strip -%}
                <a class="s6cw-tag" href="#">{{ label }}</a>
                {%- capture entry -%}{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Style","value":{{ label | json }}}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- if jsonld_props == '' -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = entry -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = jsonld_props | append: ',' | append: entry -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign style_count = style_count | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if style_chips != blank -%}
              <div class="s6cw-attr">
                <div class="s6cw-attr-name">Style</div>
                {{ style_chips }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} ---- MOOD ---- {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if mood_raw != blank -%}
            {%- assign mood_tokens = mood_raw | first | split: '|' -%}
            {%- assign mood_count = 0 -%}
            {%- capture mood_chips -%}
              {%- for tok in mood_tokens -%}
                {%- if mood_count >= mood_take -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign trimmed = tok | strip -%}
                {%- if trimmed == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- capture label -%}{%- render 's6cw-titlecase', token: trimmed -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- assign label = label | strip -%}
                <a class="s6cw-tag" href="#">{{ label }}</a>
                {%- capture entry -%}{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Mood","value":{{ label | json }}}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- if jsonld_props == '' -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = entry -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = jsonld_props | append: ',' | append: entry -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign mood_count = mood_count | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if mood_chips != blank -%}
              <div class="s6cw-attr">
                <div class="s6cw-attr-name">Mood</div>
                {{ mood_chips }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} ---- SUBJECT (from cowork.keywords) ---- {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if keywords_raw != blank -%}
            {%- assign subject_tokens = keywords_raw | first | split: '|' -%}
            {%- assign subject_count = 0 -%}
            {%- capture subject_chips -%}
              {%- for tok in subject_tokens -%}
                {%- if subject_count >= subject_take -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign trimmed = tok | strip -%}
                {%- if trimmed == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- capture label -%}{%- render 's6cw-titlecase', token: trimmed -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- assign label = label | strip -%}
                <a class="s6cw-tag" href="#">{{ label }}</a>
                {%- capture entry -%}{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Subject","value":{{ label | json }}}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- if jsonld_props == '' -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = entry -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = jsonld_props | append: ',' | append: entry -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign subject_count = subject_count | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if subject_chips != blank -%}
              <div class="s6cw-attr">
                <div class="s6cw-attr-name">Subject</div>
                {{ subject_chips }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} ---- PALETTE ----
            Known-color tokens render as swatches (and add a JSON-LD
            entry). Unknown tokens (e.g. "monochrome", "warm") fall
            through into the inline caption — palette characteristics,
            not literal colors.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if palette_raw != blank -%}
            {%- assign palette_tokens = palette_raw | first | split: '|' -%}
            {%- assign palette_caption = '' -%}
            {%- capture palette_swatches -%}
              {%- for tok in palette_tokens -%}
                {%- assign trimmed = tok | strip | downcase -%}
                {%- if trimmed == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign hex = '' -%}
                {%- case trimmed -%}
                  {%- when 'orange'     -%}{%- assign hex = '#d97333' -%}
                  {%- when 'terracotta' -%}{%- assign hex = '#c8612e' -%}
                  {%- when 'rust'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#b85c2c' -%}
                  {%- when 'red'        -%}{%- assign hex = '#c0392b' -%}
                  {%- when 'pink'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#e89dac' -%}
                  {%- when 'coral'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#e8806e' -%}
                  {%- when 'peach'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#f0b390' -%}
                  {%- when 'yellow'     -%}{%- assign hex = '#e8b94d' -%}
                  {%- when 'gold'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#c9a032' -%}
                  {%- when 'mustard'    -%}{%- assign hex = '#c89a3a' -%}
                  {%- when 'green'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#5a8a5b' -%}
                  {%- when 'olive'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#7a7a3a' -%}
                  {%- when 'sage'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#9fb39f' -%}
                  {%- when 'teal'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#3a8a85' -%}
                  {%- when 'blue'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#2f5b8a' -%}
                  {%- when 'navy'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#1a2740' -%}
                  {%- when 'purple'     -%}{%- assign hex = '#6b4a8a' -%}
                  {%- when 'lavender'   -%}{%- assign hex = '#b6a8d1' -%}
                  {%- when 'brown'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#8a5a3a' -%}
                  {%- when 'tan'        -%}{%- assign hex = '#c9a484' -%}
                  {%- when 'beige'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#e8dcc9' -%}
                  {%- when 'cream'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#f4ead8' -%}
                  {%- when 'ivory'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#f7f1e3' -%}
                  {%- when 'gray'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#888888' -%}
                  {%- when 'grey'       -%}{%- assign hex = '#888888' -%}
                  {%- when 'charcoal'   -%}{%- assign hex = '#3a3a3a' -%}
                  {%- when 'black'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#1a1a1a' -%}
                  {%- when 'white'      -%}{%- assign hex = '#f4f1ec' -%}
                {%- endcase -%}
                {%- capture name -%}{%- render 's6cw-titlecase', token: trimmed -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {%- assign name = name | strip -%}
                {%- if hex != '' -%}
                  <div class="s6cw-swatch">
                    <div class="s6cw-swatch-dot" style="background:{{ hex }}"></div>
                    <div class="s6cw-swatch-name">{{ name }}</div>
                  </div>
                  {%- capture entry -%}{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Palette","value":{{ name | json }}}{%- endcapture -%}
                  {%- if jsonld_props == '' -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = entry -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign jsonld_props = jsonld_props | append: ',' | append: entry -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- if palette_caption == '' -%}
                    {%- assign palette_caption = name -%}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- assign palette_caption = palette_caption | append: ', ' | append: name -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if palette_swatches != blank or palette_caption != blank -%}
              <div class="s6cw-attr">
                <div class="s6cw-attr-name">Palette</div>
                <div class="s6cw-swatch-line">
                  {%- if palette_swatches != blank -%}
                    <div class="s6cw-swatches">{{ palette_swatches }}</div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if palette_caption != blank -%}
                    <div class="s6cw-palette-note">{{ palette_caption }}</div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

        {%- endcapture -%}

        {%- assign aesthetic_clean = aesthetic_inner | strip -%}
        {%- if aesthetic_clean != blank -%}
          <section class="s6cw-aesthetic" aria-label="Aesthetic">
            <h2>Aesthetic</h2>
            {{ aesthetic_inner }}
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}

      </div>{%- comment -%} /.s6cw-buy {%- endcomment -%}
    </div>{%- comment -%} /.s6cw-product {%- endcomment -%}
  </main>

  <hr class="s6cw-rule">

  {%- comment -%} ============================================================
    COLLAPSIBLE CONTENT SECTIONS
    All panel content is in the DOM on load (SEO/AI-safe). JS only
    toggles aria-expanded + an is-open class. Do not lazy-load.
    Items hide entirely when their data isn't available.
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}

  <div class="s6cw-accordion">

    {%- comment -%} ---- ABOUT THIS PIECE ----
      Two states from the brief:
      A) Artist wrote a description (product.description not blank)
         -> their words lead, attributed to them.
      B) Artist silent, Cowork summary present
         -> Cowork summary fills it, with the quiet AI attribution.
      Both states already in the DOM; whichever one matches renders.
      C) Neither -> the whole item hides.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign artist_description = product.description | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- if artist_description != blank or cw_summary != blank -%}
      <div class="s6cw-acc-item">
        <button class="s6cw-acc-head" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="s6cwPanelAbout" type="button">
          About This Piece <span class="s6cw-acc-sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="s6cw-acc-panel is-open" id="s6cwPanelAbout">
          <div class="s6cw-acc-inner">
            {%- if artist_description != blank -%}
              <div class="s6cw-about-body">{{ product.description }}</div>
              <div class="s6cw-ai-note">
                <span class="s6cw-ai-dot"></span>
                Description by the artist{%- if artist_name != blank -%}, {{ artist_name }}{%- endif -%}.
              </div>
            {%- elsif cw_summary != blank -%}
              <p class="s6cw-about-body">{{ cw_summary }}</p>
              <div class="s6cw-ai-note">
                <span class="s6cw-ai-dot"></span>
                Visual description generated by Society6 AI from the artwork.
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---- MEET THE ARTIST ----
      Gated on artist.bio. No bio -> no section. See port notes for
      the production data dependency on the artist namespace.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if artist_bio != blank -%}
      <div class="s6cw-acc-item">
        <button class="s6cw-acc-head" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="s6cwPanelArtist" type="button">
          Meet the Artist <span class="s6cw-acc-sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="s6cw-acc-panel is-open" id="s6cwPanelArtist">
          <div class="s6cw-acc-inner">
            <div class="s6cw-artist">
              {%- if artist_avatar != blank -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  artist.avatar is a url-type metafield holding a direct
                  image URL. Rendered as-is — no image_url filter, since
                  it's a string not a Shopify file_reference. Production
                  should swap to file_reference and use | image_url.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <img src="{{ artist_avatar | escape }}" alt="{{ artist_name | default: 'Artist' | escape }}" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy">
              {%- endif -%}
              <div>
                {%- if artist_name != blank -%}
                  <div class="s6cw-artist-name">{{ artist_name }}</div>
                {%- endif -%}
                <div class="s6cw-artist-bio">{{ artist_bio }}</div>
                {%- if artist_url != blank -%}
                  <a class="s6cw-artist-link" href="{{ artist_url }}">Visit artist shop →</a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} ---- SPECIFICATIONS ----
      Template-static per the brief (Bucket A). Genuinely identical
      for every canvas print — catalog-wide boilerplate, not per-
      product data. Always present because the template supplies the
      text. If production later wants per-product specs, this becomes
      a metafield-driven block; flag it, don't build it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="s6cw-acc-item">
      <button class="s6cw-acc-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="s6cwPanelSpecs" type="button">
        Specifications <span class="s6cw-acc-sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="s6cw-acc-panel" id="s6cwPanelSpecs">
        <div class="s6cw-acc-inner">
          <ul class="s6cw-specs">
            <li>Bright white, fine cotton-poly blend matte canvas.</li>
            <li>Gallery-quality ink for rich, deep saturation.</li>
            <li>Hand-stretched canvas over pine stretcher bars.</li>
            <li>Framed canvas prints include hanging hardware.</li>
            <li>Made in the USA.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---- SHIPPING & RETURNS ----
      Template-static per the brief (Bucket A). Same reasoning as
      Specifications.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="s6cw-acc-item">
      <button class="s6cw-acc-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="s6cwPanelShip" type="button">
        Shipping &amp; Returns <span class="s6cw-acc-sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="s6cw-acc-panel" id="s6cwPanelShip">
        <div class="s6cw-acc-inner">
          <p class="s6cw-about-body" style="margin-bottom:14px;">
            <strong>Shipping.</strong> Items are made to order and typically ship within 3&ndash;4 business days.
          </p>
          <p class="s6cw-about-body">
            <strong>Returns.</strong> Return requests can be made within 30 days of your item's delivery &mdash; no stress, no hassle.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <hr class="s6cw-rule">

  {%- comment -%} ===== ENRICHMENT 3: MORE LIKE THIS (stub) =====
    Production gap from the prototype. Real implementation would
    query metadata-similar products (overlap on cowork tags) with
    a category/artist fallback. Until that exists, render four
    visual placeholders so the page composition is intact.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="s6cw-section">
    <h2 class="s6cw-h2">More like this</h2>
    <span class="s6cw-stub-flag">Prototype stub — production gap</span>
    <div class="s6cw-similar-grid">
      {%- assign similar_labels = 'Shared tags: cat · line-art · minimalist,Shared tags: warm tones · geometric,Shared tags: mid-century modern · abstract,Shared tags: whimsical · illustration' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for label in similar_labels -%}
        <a class="s6cw-similar-card" href="#">
          <div class="ph">{{ label }}</div>
          <div class="cap">Metadata-similar product</div>
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

</article>

{%- comment -%} ============================================================
  JSON-LD STRUCTURED DATA
  Rendered server-side from the same metafields that drive the
  on-page chips. Consistency rule from the brief: additionalProperty
  contains exactly the visible chips/swatches — no more, no less.
  This is the crawl-time copy. No second copy gets generated at
  runtime because the on-page render and this script share one
  source of truth (the metafields).
============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Product",
  "name": {{ product.title | json }},
  "image": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
  "description": {{ cw_summary | default: product.description | strip_html | json }},
  "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": "Society6" },
  "category": {{ product.product_type | default: 'Art Print' | json }},
  {%- if artist_name != blank %}
  "creator": { "@type": "Person", "name": {{ artist_name | json }} },
  {%- endif %}
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "price": {{ product.price | money_without_currency | strip_html | json }},
    "priceCurrency": {{ cart.currency.iso_code | json }},
    "availability": {%- if product.available -%}"https://schema.org/InStock"{%- else -%}"https://schema.org/OutOfStock"{%- endif -%},
    "url": {{ shop.url | append: product.url | json }}
  }{%- if jsonld_props != blank -%},
  "additionalProperty": [{{ jsonld_props }}]
  {%- endif %}
}
</script>

{%- comment -%} ============================================================
  THUMB SWITCHER + ACCORDION TOGGLE
  Scoped to .s6cw-page. Pure DOM toggling — no fetches, no lazy
  loading, no content removal. Accessible: aria-expanded reflects
  state.
============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
<script>
(function(){
  var page = document.querySelector('.s6cw-page[data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"]');
  if (!page) return;

  // Thumb switcher
  var hero = page.querySelector('#s6cwHero');
  var thumbs = page.querySelectorAll('#s6cwThumbs img');
  thumbs.forEach(function(t){
    t.addEventListener('click', function(){
      var full = t.getAttribute('data-full');
      if (full && hero) hero.setAttribute('src', full);
      thumbs.forEach(function(c){ c.classList.remove('is-active'); });
      t.classList.add('is-active');
    });
  });

  // Accordion toggle
  page.querySelectorAll('.s6cw-acc-head').forEach(function(head){
    head.addEventListener('click', function(){
      var panelId = head.getAttribute('aria-controls');
      var panel = document.getElementById(panelId);
      if (!panel) return;
      var open = head.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      head.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!open));
      panel.classList.toggle('is-open', !open);
    });
  });

  // Static variant chips: pressed-state toggle only (prototype scope).
  page.querySelectorAll('.s6cw-opt').forEach(function(opt){
    var picks = opt.querySelectorAll('.s6cw-pick');
    picks.forEach(function(p){
      p.addEventListener('click', function(){
        picks.forEach(function(o){ o.classList.remove('is-active'); o.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false'); });
        p.classList.add('is-active');
        p.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
      });
    });
  });
})();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
/* ============================================================
   ENRICHED PDP — CSS, ported from the prototype.
   All classes are .s6cw- prefixed to avoid theme collisions.
   The typography stack is deliberately self-contained (Georgia
   serif + Helvetica Neue sans) so the page reads as the refined
   retail minimalism the prototype defined, not the host theme's
   tokens. On the production port, swap these CSS variables for
   the Society6 | Production design system tokens.
   ============================================================ */
.s6cw-page {
  --s6cw-ink: #1a1a1a;
  --s6cw-ink-soft: #555150;
  --s6cw-ink-faint: #8c8784;
  --s6cw-paper: #ffffff;
  --s6cw-paper-warm: #f7f4f0;
  --s6cw-line: #e6e1da;
  --s6cw-accent: #c8612e;
  --s6cw-accent-soft: #f0e3d8;
  --s6cw-radius: 10px;
  --s6cw-maxw: 1180px;
  --s6cw-serif: 'Georgia', 'Times New Roman', serif;
  --s6cw-sans: 'Helvetica Neue', 'Arial', sans-serif;

  font-family: var(--s6cw-sans);
  color: var(--s6cw-ink);
  background: var(--s6cw-paper);
  line-height: 1.6;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
.s6cw-page * { box-sizing: border-box; }
.s6cw-page img { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
.s6cw-page a { color: inherit; }

.s6cw-wrap { max-width: var(--s6cw-maxw); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px; }

/* breadcrumb */
.s6cw-crumb {
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  padding: 14px 0;
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
}
.s6cw-crumb a { text-decoration: none; }
.s6cw-crumb a:hover { color: var(--s6cw-accent); }
.s6cw-crumb span { margin: 0 6px; }

/* product layout — single column mobile, two column ≥860px */
.s6cw-product { display: block; padding-bottom: 8px; }
@media (min-width: 860px) {
  .s6cw-product {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: start;
  }
}

/* gallery */
.s6cw-gallery-main {
  background: var(--s6cw-paper-warm);
  border-radius: var(--s6cw-radius);
  overflow: hidden;
  border: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
}
.s6cw-gallery-main img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1/1; object-fit: cover; }
.s6cw-thumbs { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 10px; }
.s6cw-thumbs img {
  width: 72px; height: 72px; object-fit: cover;
  border-radius: 6px;
  border: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color 0.18s ease;
}
.s6cw-thumbs img:hover,
.s6cw-thumbs img.is-active { border-color: var(--s6cw-accent); }
@media (min-width: 860px) {
  .s6cw-gallery { position: sticky; top: 24px; }
}

/* buy column */
.s6cw-buy { padding-top: 24px; }
@media (min-width: 860px) { .s6cw-buy { padding-top: 0; } }

.s6cw-title {
  font-family: var(--s6cw-serif);
  font-size: 30px;
  line-height: 1.18;
  font-weight: 400;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  margin: 0;
}
@media (min-width: 860px) { .s6cw-title { font-size: 36px; } }

.s6cw-byline {
  margin-top: 8px;
  font-size: 14px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-soft);
}
.s6cw-byline a, .s6cw-byline-name {
  color: var(--s6cw-accent);
  text-decoration: none;
  font-weight: 600;
}
.s6cw-byline a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

.s6cw-price {
  font-size: 24px;
  margin: 18px 0 4px;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.s6cw-opt { margin-top: 20px; }
.s6cw-opt-label {
  font-size: 12px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.s6cw-opt-label b { color: var(--s6cw-ink); font-weight: 600; }
.s6cw-chips-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
.s6cw-pick {
  border: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
  background: var(--s6cw-paper);
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 9px 14px;
  font-size: 13px;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-family: inherit;
  transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink);
}
.s6cw-pick:hover { border-color: var(--s6cw-ink-soft); }
.s6cw-pick.is-active {
  border-color: var(--s6cw-ink);
  background: var(--s6cw-ink);
  color: var(--s6cw-paper);
}

.s6cw-cart-form { margin: 0; }
.s6cw-cart {
  margin-top: 24px;
  width: 100%;
  background: var(--s6cw-ink);
  color: var(--s6cw-paper);
  border: none;
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 16px;
  font-size: 15px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-family: inherit;
  transition: background 0.18s ease;
}
.s6cw-cart:hover { background: var(--s6cw-accent); }
.s6cw-cart[disabled] { opacity: 0.6; cursor: not-allowed; }

.s6cw-reassure {
  margin-top: 14px;
  font-size: 12.5px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 4px;
}

/* aesthetic block */
.s6cw-aesthetic {
  margin-top: 20px;
  padding: 16px 16px 14px;
  background: var(--s6cw-paper-warm);
  border: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
  border-radius: var(--s6cw-radius);
}
.s6cw-aesthetic h2 {
  font-size: 12px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  font-weight: 600;
  margin: 0 0 10px;
}
.s6cw-attr { margin-bottom: 9px; }
.s6cw-attr:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.s6cw-attr-name {
  font-size: 11px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  margin-bottom: 5px;
}
.s6cw-tag {
  display: inline-block;
  text-decoration: none;
  font-size: 12.5px;
  padding: 4px 11px;
  border-radius: 100px;
  background: var(--s6cw-paper);
  border: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
  color: var(--s6cw-ink);
  margin: 0 5px 5px 0;
  transition: border-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
}
.s6cw-tag:hover { border-color: var(--s6cw-accent); color: var(--s6cw-accent); }

.s6cw-swatch-line {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 12px;
}
.s6cw-swatches { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.s6cw-swatch { text-align: center; }
.s6cw-swatch-dot {
  width: 30px; height: 30px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
  margin-bottom: 3px;
}
.s6cw-swatch-name {
  font-size: 10px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}
.s6cw-palette-note {
  font-size: 11.5px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  font-style: italic;
}

/* sections + rules */
.s6cw-section {
  max-width: var(--s6cw-maxw);
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 40px 16px;
}
.s6cw-rule {
  max-width: var(--s6cw-maxw);
  margin: 8px auto 0;
  border: none;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
}
.s6cw-h2 {
  font-family: var(--s6cw-serif);
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: 400;
  margin: 0 0 16px;
}

.s6cw-about-body {
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.7;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink);
  max-width: 640px;
  margin: 0;
}
.s6cw-ai-note {
  margin-top: 12px;
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
}
.s6cw-ai-dot {
  width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--s6cw-accent);
  flex: none;
}

/* artist row */
.s6cw-artist {
  display: flex;
  gap: 16px;
  align-items: flex-start;
  margin-top: 4px;
  padding: 20px;
  background: var(--s6cw-paper-warm);
  border-radius: var(--s6cw-radius);
  max-width: 640px;
}
.s6cw-artist img {
  width: 56px; height: 56px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  flex: none;
}
.s6cw-artist-name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; }
.s6cw-artist-bio {
  font-size: 14px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-soft);
  margin-top: 3px;
  white-space: pre-line;
}
.s6cw-artist-link {
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--s6cw-accent);
  text-decoration: none;
  font-weight: 600;
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: 7px;
}
.s6cw-artist-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

/* specs list */
.s6cw-specs { list-style: none; padding: 0; max-width: 640px; margin: 0; }
.s6cw-specs li {
  font-size: 14px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink-soft);
  padding: 8px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
}
.s6cw-specs li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

/* accordion */
.s6cw-accordion {
  max-width: var(--s6cw-maxw);
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 8px 16px 0;
}
/* The rule directly below the accordion sits flush against the last item,
   so the gap below "Shipping & Returns" matches the 22px inter-item spacing.
   Scoped via adjacent-sibling so the OTHER .s6cw-rule (between the product
   grid and the accordion) keeps its 8px breathing room. */
.s6cw-accordion + .s6cw-rule { margin-top: 0; }
.s6cw-acc-item { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line); }
.s6cw-acc-item:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line); }
.s6cw-acc-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; } /* prevents stacking with the section <hr> below */
.s6cw-acc-head {
  width: 100%;
  background: none;
  border: none;
  font-family: var(--s6cw-serif);
  font-size: 21px;
  color: var(--s6cw-ink);
  text-align: left;
  padding: 22px 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 16px;
}
.s6cw-acc-head:hover { color: var(--s6cw-accent); }
.s6cw-acc-sign {
  flex: none;
  width: 22px; height: 22px;
  position: relative;
}
.s6cw-acc-sign::before,
.s6cw-acc-sign::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  background: var(--s6cw-ink-soft);
  transition: transform 0.22s ease, opacity 0.22s ease;
}
.s6cw-acc-sign::before {
  top: 50%; left: 0; right: 0; height: 1.5px;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
}
.s6cw-acc-sign::after {
  left: 50%; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 1.5px;
  transform: translateX(-50%);
}
.s6cw-acc-head[aria-expanded="true"] .s6cw-acc-sign::after {
  transform: translateX(-50%) scaleY(0);
  opacity: 0;
}
.s6cw-acc-head[aria-expanded="true"] .s6cw-acc-sign::before {
  background: var(--s6cw-accent);
}
.s6cw-acc-panel {
  overflow: hidden;
  max-height: 0;
  min-height: 0;
  transition: max-height 0.28s ease;
}
.s6cw-acc-panel.is-open { max-height: 1600px; }
/* Closed panel contributes zero height — no padding, no min-height. */
.s6cw-acc-inner { padding: 0; }
/* Padding only kicks in when the panel is open. */
.s6cw-acc-panel.is-open .s6cw-acc-inner { padding: 2px 4px 26px; }

/* more like this */
.s6cw-similar-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  gap: 14px;
}
@media (min-width: 640px) {
  .s6cw-similar-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
}
.s6cw-similar-card {
  border: 1px solid var(--s6cw-line);
  border-radius: var(--s6cw-radius);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: inherit;
  display: block;
}
.s6cw-similar-card .ph {
  aspect-ratio: 1/1;
  background: repeating-linear-gradient(
    45deg, var(--s6cw-paper-warm), var(--s6cw-paper-warm) 11px,
    var(--s6cw-accent-soft) 11px, var(--s6cw-accent-soft) 22px);
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  font-size: 11px; color: var(--s6cw-ink-faint);
  text-align: center; padding: 10px;
}
.s6cw-similar-card .cap { padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 12.5px; }

.s6cw-stub-flag {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--s6cw-accent);
  border: 1px dashed var(--s6cw-accent);
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 3px 8px;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
}
{% endstylesheet %}

